[[!comment format=mdwn
 username="joey"
 subject="""comment 4"""
 date="2026-10-07T20:24:44Z"
 content="""
	continuing transition [\"forget git history\",\"forget dead remotes\"]

If your local git-annex branch contains a `git-annex forget` transition,
git-annex necessarily cannot merge unrelated remote git-annex branches into it,
because they may contain exactly the historical information that was requested
to be forgotten. Instead, the new information is extracted from the remote
git-annex branch and put into the local git-annex branch.

Once the local git-annex branch is pushed to the remote as synced/git-annex,
and git-annex is run on the server, it will replace the unrelated git-annex
branch.
"""]]
